     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** See why the regression coefficient $\\theta$ is not the elasticity: the elasticity is $\\theta$ scaled by $\\partial p/\\partial m = 1/(1+m)^2$, which falls as immigrants already make up more of the cell.\n- **Model.** A view of [Immigrant Share Elasticity Model](note:immigrant-share-elasticity-model).\n- **Elements.** Panel `elasticity`: curve `elast`; point `probe` (draggable, bound to `m0`); line `thetaline`. Readouts `e0_out`, `p0_out`, `dw10_out`.\n- **Tests.** Python: $-0.572/1.168^2 = -0.4193$, $-0.572/4 = -0.143$."
      }
     ],
     "words": 60,
     "symbols": [
      "$m$",
      "$p$",
      "$\\theta$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
